# Repo health and audits

## When the user asks for an audit

Run a **full pass**: lint, typecheck, build, and tests. Fix straightforward issues (unused imports, dead code, obvious inconsistencies). Call out anything needing **product or security** decisions instead of guessing.

## After major milestones

- Confirm **README** (or the project’s main doc) still matches how to run, configure `.env`, and use connectors. Update only if behavior or env vars changed.
- If dependencies were bumped or added, note **security/outdated** concerns if `npm audit` (or equivalent) shows actionable high-severity items relevant to this app.

## Optional multi-model review

If the user uses **parallel agents** or external review (MCP): treat review output as **issues to resolve or explicitly defer**, not noise to ignore.
